        "original_id": "dc646f08-a4f1-5ead-87bd-f3c1d210b7b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincent Sherman, David Seltzer, David L. Wolper, Walon Green, William Dozier\n- Films: Mr. Skeffington, Nora Prentiss, The Young Philadelphians, The Omen, Bird on a Wire, Lucas, Punchline, Shining Through, Harriet Craig, The Hellstrom Chronicle\n- Companies: Columbia Pictures\n- Roles: director, producer, screenwriter\n- Awards: Writers Guild of America Award nomination\n\nFacts:\n- Vincent Sherman directed the films \"Mr. Skeffington\" in 1944, \"Nora Prentiss\" in 1947, and \"The Young Philadelphians\" in 1959.\n- David Seltzer, born in 1940, is an American screenwriter, producer, and director.\n- David Seltzer wrote the screenplay for \"The Omen\" in 1976.\n- \"The Hellstrom Chronicle\" was conceived and produced by David L. Wolper, directed by Walon Green, and written by David Seltzer, who received a Writers Guild of America Award nomination for the screenplay.\n- David Seltzer wrote the screenplay for \"Bird on a Wire\" in 1990.\n- As writer-director, David Seltzer made the 1986 film \"Lucas,\" the 1988 film \"Punchline,\" and the 1992 film \"Shining Through.\"\n- The film \"Harriet Craig\" was directed by Vincent Sherman, produced by William Dozier, and distributed by Columbia Pictures.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
